# Review routing: a card change requests its owner automatically, so a
# submission never sits unassigned waiting for someone to notice it.
#
# The corpus is the reviewed artefact — schema, engines and docs can move
# faster, but a card is what gets cited, so it is what needs an owner.
#
# Note for whoever edits this next: GitHub silently ignores an owner it cannot
# resolve. A typo here does not error — it just stops requesting reviewers,
# while the file still looks configured. Verify any change by opening a PR that
# touches cards/ and confirming a reviewer is auto-assigned.

/cards/                 @arsalan-akhtar
/schema/                @arsalan-akhtar
/mcp-server/src/cards/  @arsalan-akhtar
